<header><p class="st-kicker">tribal confederation · South America</p><h1 class="st-title">Araucanía</h1><p class="st-meta">1550 CE – 1883 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The lands of the Mapuche south of the Biobío river, which resisted Spanish conquest for three centuries and kept their independence until the 1880s.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>When <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pedro-de-valdivia">Pedro de Valdivia</a> advanced south from <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/spanish-jamaica">Santiago</a> in 1550, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mapuche">Mapuche</a> of the region between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/biobio-river">Biobío</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tolten-river">Toltén</a> rivers rose against him. Under leaders such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lautaro">Lautaro</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caupolican">Caupolicán</a> they defeated and killed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valdivia">Valdivia</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-tucapel">Tucapel</a> in 1553, beginning the long <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arauco-war">Arauco War</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mapuche">Mapuche</a> had no central state. Each lineage was led by a lonko, and groups united under war leaders called toqui in times of conflict. After the victory at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-curalaba">Curalaba</a> in 1598, Mapuche forces destroyed the Spanish towns south of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/biobio-river">Biobío</a>. At the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/parliament-of-quillin">Parliament of Quillín</a> in 1641 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> recognised the river as the frontier, and later parlamentos regulated trade and peace. The Mapuche adopted horses and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cattle">cattle</a> and traded across the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/andecavi">Andes</a> into the pampas.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Independent <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-chile">Chile</a> carried out the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/occupation-of-araucania">Occupation of Araucanía</a> from 1861 to 1883, while <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argentina">Argentina's</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/conquest-of-the-desert">Conquest of the Desert</a> subdued the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mapuche">Mapuche</a> east of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/andecavi">Andes</a>. Mapuche lands were confiscated and confined to reservations, and land claims remain a major political issue.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="tribal confederation, 1550 CE – 1883 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><ellipse cx="44" cy="56" rx="16" ry="24"/><path d="M44 34 V78"/><path d="M68 20 V84"/><path d="M68 20 L63 30 H73 Z"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">tribal confederation</p><p class="st-emblem-region">South America</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:90.55%;width:6.63%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1550 CE – 1883 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>tribal confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Lautaro, Caupolicán, Pelantaro</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Mapuche religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Mapudungun</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/chile">Chile</a>, <a href="/countries/argentina">Argentina</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Mapuche lands, Wallmapu, Mapuche</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1716&amp;focus=araucania" aria-label="Araucanía on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="2879 3548 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Araucanía lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M3195 3647h0M3195 3647h0M3201 3813h0"/><path